CHANGELOG.md:13:- Added new browser model registry entries for LFM 2.6B, LFM 2.5 1.2B, Bonsai 27B, and Maple Preview, alongside existing Gemma 4 options, with usage notes and download size metadata for on-device selection.
CHANGELOG.md:57:- Added responsive scaling and centering for fixed-size Hyperframes compositions inside chat and artifact iframes.
CHANGELOG.md:161:- Made inline artifact previews optionally single-card so new lesson plans, maps, animations, and other artifacts can replace the previous preview instead of stacking in the chat chrome.
CHANGELOG.md:328:- Added OpenAI image-model support to the `generate_image` browser tool, with model, size, quality, mode, and diagram-kind controls plus browser-local SVG fallback.
CHANGELOG.md:380:- Added a resizable session sidebar in the web chat with a draggable column-resize handle that persists its width to `localStorage` between sessions.
CHANGELOG.md:393:- The desktop sidebar collapse toggle was removed in favor of the new drag-resize handle; the mobile drawer toggle is unchanged.
CHANGELOG.md:463:- New "Speech & Voice" tab in Settings with a provider abstraction. Built-in providers: Gemini Live (existing, refactored), OpenAI TTS (`gpt-4o-mini-tts`, `tts-1`, `tts-1-hd`), OpenAI Realtime (WebRTC duplex, preview), and Supertonic-3 (local ONNX, experimental — sessions load, synthesis pipeline pending). Users can also add OpenAI-compatible custom TTS endpoints inline.
CHANGELOG.md:469:- Chat-page header icons (new session, history, settings, share, usage, speech, artifacts) now show together at sm/md/lg sizes instead of disappearing at md; the hamburger collapses to xs only, and its dropdown gained the previously missing "New session" / "Session history" entries.
CHANGELOG.md:484:- The default shell provider is now `google` with `gemini-3.1-pro-preview`.
CHANGELOG.md:504:- The install wrapper script at `~/.local/bin/keating` now uses `exec node ...` to invoke `bin/keating.js` instead of trying to `exec` a standalone binary that does not exist in the tarball.
CHANGELOG.md:600:- `web:build` and `web:preview` tasks for production builds
